{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DECISIONS APPROVED (operator, 2026-07-24): (A) stands — local never signs. The conflicting manifest.py:206-207 back-out sentence is a verbatim mirror of ADR 0002's S4b back-out paragraph; both read as reader-side tolerance for attestations that lack verified_at_sha (which pre-S4b attestations genuinely are), not authorization to mint new ones. Applying the record-of-deliberate-change test: the root cause is a sequencing accident (source stamped after the sign decision), no ADR/commit decided local should sign in plan review, and no test pins it as a feature. Both prose sites will say 'pre-S4b' instead of 'local mode or pre-S4b'. Completeness gap closes at the SIGNING SEAM: no new signed attestation may carry verified_at_sha=None (legacy read-tolerance unchanged), which resign/sign-review and drift-refresh re-sign inherit for free; the REVIEW_RESULT sidecar additionally records source for auditability. Lands AFTER 72d9 (athletic-esthetical-polecat), rebased on its fix. WIP 5bf846df9 backed up to ~/rebar-5128-wip-5bf846df9.bundle."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1784951719412289001,"uuid":"88a604e1-b597-43f3-812b-c84719505453"}